From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:09:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/52] Add pin colors to the default KiCad schematic
 colorscheme

Pin.to_svg() uses colorscheme.pin_names and colorscheme.pin_numbers,
which the tmTheme colorschemes have but the default KiCad one lacked, so
exporting any pin with it failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013wvKon1yvwjNtAdtSuZzZh
---
 src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic_colors.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic_colors.py b/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic_colors.py
index d38a88d..1c84187 100644
--- a/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic_colors.py
+++ b/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic_colors.py
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ class Colorscheme:
         text = 'black'
         values = 'black'
         labels = 'black'
+        pin_names = 'black'
+        pin_numbers = 'black'
         fill = '#cccccc'
         background = 'white'
 
